  "summary": "Skye Kakoschke-Moore, a senator from the Nick Xenophon Team (NXT), has announced her resignation from the Australian Senate after discovering she holds dual British citizenship by descent through her mother. The revelation came after receiving confirmation from the UK Home Office and legal experts. Although she believed she was not eligible for British citizenship based on earlier advice received during her childhood, she learned that her mother's birth in Singapore (a former British colony) and subsequent citizenship status made Skye a British citizen by descent. Kakoschke-Moore intends to refer the matter to the high court to determine how her Senate vacancy will be filled. She also expressed her intent to remain active in the NXT and possibly return to the Senate. A recount of the 2016 Senate election could result in Tim Storrer, another NXT candidate, taking her seat. Nick Xenophon commented that the situation is legally complex and noted this may not mark the end of Kakoschke-Moore's political career."
}
```

